      "section": "physics",
      "topic": "Electrostatics & Capacitors",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "question": "A parallel-plate capacitor has capacitance C₀ with air. Over the left half of the plate area, a slab of dielectric constant 3 fills the whole gap; over the right half, a slab of dielectric constant 3 fills half the gap thickness (the rest is air). The new capacitance is",
      "options": [
        "2C₀",
        "3C₀/2",
        "9C₀/4",
        "5C₀/2"
      ],
      "answer": 2,
      "explanation": "Left half: 3 × C₀/2 = 3C₀/2. Right half: air and dielectric in series, C = (C₀/2) × 2K/(K + 1) = (C₀/2)(6/4) = 3C₀/4. The halves are in parallel: 3C₀/2 + 3C₀/4 = 9C₀/4.",
